Subject: [PATCH] J714s release 9: kernel v272-17, firmware j714s14,
 hyprland-m5 0.57.2-4 and Aura 0008 (m1n1-aurora v272-4)

Re-pinned from betizzel/omarchy-m5:
- linux-aurora 7.3.0.aurora17.v272-17 (6d7adebd..., 44463376 bytes) from
  d89b688: aurora-silicon/linux integration/aurora 677be395 plus
  patches/j714s-27.2/linux 0001-0020. CONFIG_APPLE_SOC_SLEEP stays off.
  The qualification pins follow 7.3.0-17.v272-17-ARCH.
- omarchy-aurora-firmware 20261014.j714s14 (d50de8e7..., 55694 bytes)
  from eb98945: aurora_drv_video.so for VA-API decode by default.
- hyprland-m5 0.57.2-4 from 6e48e58 (chrisohearn's #24, degenerate EDID
  primaries treated as missing): the aarch64 .pkg.tar.xz (ec014c6a...)
  recompressed to zstd with the same tar inside (396e77cb...),
  38e8bbfd..., 51121267 bytes.
- m1n1-aurora 1.6.1.aurora24.v272-4 (4436dcd1..., 2427423 bytes) from
  7306169 (chrisohearn's #18, Aura 0008).
Nothing else changes. Set j714s-dev-runtime-7bb16931891c.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
